				\begin{document}$${FE} \; \% \;=\frac{2{cVF}}{Q}\times 100 \% $$\end{document}FE%=2cVFQ×100%where c and V are the H2O2 concentration and the volume of the electrolyte in the cathode (30 or 260 mL), F is the Faraday constant, and Q is the total charge passed.

