To evaluate the kinetic energy barrier of the ORR, we used a constrained ab initio molecular dynamics (AIMD) method, the “slow growth” method, to obtain the free energy profile at 300 K through different collective variable30,31. A cut-off energy of 400 eV, a k-mesh grid of 1 × 1 × 1, a time step of 0.5 fs and a canonical ensemble (NVT) were adopted in the AIMD simulations. The whole system contained 24 H2O molecules and one OH– in the bulk water to model the alkaline environment. The final stabilized solution network was obtained by performing AIMD simulations of the system at 300 K and optimized the geometry structure. In this method, the value of the reaction coordinate ξ is linearly changed from the characteristic value of the initial state (IS) to that of the transition state (TS) with a velocity of transformation \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
